  "notes": "The header names Dietmund as the giver but the walkthrough never has you speak to him: both the opening and the closing interaction are with the Door: Merchant's House on the second floor of Lower Jeuno (G-11), and 'Door:Name' is a real markable entity the normaliser already folds to the client's spacing. Start is therefore moved to the door with the header string kept in raw -- a marker MOVE, not a removal, the same call the pilot made for Carbuncle Debacle. Shalott is the page's own '(Optional)' and only buys a cutscene. Bullet 3 is gated on game time (21:30 to 4:00), which nothing in the packets reports, and although the Description talks about bringing back the flower's roots the walkthrough never names a key item for them, so this quest carries NO evidence anywhere and the ladder is four unobservable clicks resting on the session latch. Inventing a roots key item to fill the gap is exactly the guessing this rebuild exists to avoid. The Kraken sub-bullet is a warning about a level 37-38 aggressor above the flowers, and the 'Looks like nobody's home' sub-bullet under 4 is post-completion flavour; neither is a step.",
