  "notes": "Three bullets, and the middle one is five trades to NPCs the page names only as 'Resistance Fighter'. That is a real name and it folds to a key, so every NPC carrying it draws at once -- which is what you want here, since the five are done in any order -- but it is a SHARED name and not five distinguishable targets, so it is ONE step carrying five Soothing Potions rather than five steps a player could never tell apart or a group whose members are all the same row. Nothing in this quest is observable: no key item is granted at any point and the reward is Cruor or a random Evolith, so the whole ladder rests on the session latch and the potions are its only readiness signal. The header writes the giver 'Rashid' and the walkthrough 'Rashid (A)'; both fold to the same key and the wiki form is used, as the guide says for Abyssea NPCs. 'Zoning is not required to repeat' and the line about re-speaking to Rashid to reinitiate the log are repeat mechanics, not steps. Fame 'akon' is an Abyssea zone code rather than one of the nine regions and gates nothing.",
